  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This makes 6 portions and takes about 1 hour 35 minutes. The thing to watch is the batter: it should be thick enough to hold its shape in the parcel but pour in. If too thick it will not steam evenly through the centre; if too thin it never sets properly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The palm oil must be warmed to a liquid before blending it in. Cold or solid palm oil will not incorporate evenly and leaves orange streaks through the finished koki."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 6,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "black-eyed-beans",
              "amount": 400,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "soaked overnight, drained and peeled",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "palm-oil",
              "amount": 5,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "warmed until liquid",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "spinach",
              "amount": 150,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "blanched and finely chopped",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chilli-red",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "scotch bonnet or to taste",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "coriander-fresh",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "small bunch",
              "prepNote": "finely chopped",
              "isOptional": true,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "water",
              "amount": 100,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": "as needed for blending",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Peel the soaked beans by rubbing in water and skimming off the skins. Drain well."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blanch the spinach in boiling water for 1 minute. Drain, squeeze out excess water, and chop finely."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend the peeled beans with the chilli and a little water until very smooth. Use as little water as possible."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir the warm palm oil into the batter. Add the chopped spinach, coriander, and salt. Mix thoroughly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Prepare 6 squares of doubled foil. Ladle batter into each parcel, filling halfway. Fold tightly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Steam over boiling water for 55-60 minutes until firm and set when pressed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rest 10 minutes before unwrapping. Serve warm with boiled plantain, yam, or as part of a shared table."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Koki does not set firmly and stays soft in the centre",
              "cause": "Too much water in the batter or steamer temperature too low",
              "fix": "Ensure steamer is at a full boil throughout and use the minimum water when blending"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Palm oil has separated and pools at the bottom of each parcel",
              "cause": "Oil not warm enough when added or stirred in unevenly",
              "fix": "Warm palm oil until fully liquid and stir into batter vigorously for a full minute"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Strong bitter taste from the spinach",
              "cause": "Spinach not blanched before adding",
              "fix": "Blanch spinach first. It removes bitterness. Squeeze out all the water before you chop it."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Koki is a traditional dish of the Bamileke people of the western grasslands of Cameroon. It is cooked in banana leaves in the traditional version, which impart a distinctive grassy flavour to the bean cake. The dish is eaten as a side dish or as a main with boiled plantain or yam. It is one of the most nutritionally dense dishes in Central African cooking, high in protein from the beans and fat from the palm oil."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
